1. c4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. d4 d6 6. Nc3 Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. e4 c6 9. h3 Qb6 { Key: Tal takes a King's Indian structure with a strong knight on c5. } 10. d5 cxd5 11. cxd5 Nc5 12. Ne1 Bd7 13. Nd3 Nxd3 14. Qxd3 Rfc8 15. Rb1 Nh5 16. Be3 Qb4 17. Qe2 Rc4 { Key: the rooks occupy the half-open c-file; 19...f5 follows to open the kingside. } 18. Rfc1 Rac8 19. Kh2 f5 20. exf5 Bxf5 21. Ra1 Nf4 { Key: the knight sacrifice: Black gets two pawns and open lines against the h2/g2 king for the piece. } 22. gxf4 exf4 23. Bd2 { Key: Tal converts the attack into material: the e2-pawn costs White heavy material. } 23... Qxb2 24. Rab1 f3 25. Rxb2 fxe2 26. Rb3 { Key: Black emerges with the better ending and wins it by move 46. } 26... Rd4 27. Be1 Be5+ 28. Kg1 Bf4 29. Nxe2 Rxc1 30. Nxd4 Rxe1+ 31. Bf1 Be4 32. Ne2 Be5 33. f4 Bf6 34. Rxb7 Bxd5 35. Rc7 Bxa2 36. Rxa7 Bc4 37. Ra8+ Kf7 38. Ra7+ Ke6 39. Ra3 d5 40. Kf2 Bh4+ 41. Kg2 Kd6 42. Ng3 Bxg3 43. Bxc4 dxc4 44. Kxg3 Kd5 45. Ra7 c3 46. Rc7 Kd4 0-1

