1. Nf3 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. O-O Nc6 6. Nc3 d6 7. d4 a6 8. d5 Na5 9. Nd2 c5 10. Qc2 e5 { Key: White trades the dark-squared bishops to weaken Black's king. } 11. b3 Ng4 12. e4 f5 13. exf5 gxf5 14. Nd1 b5 15. f3 e4 16. Bb2 exf3 17. Bxf3 Bxb2 18. Qxb2 Ne5 19. Be2 { Key: the exchange is given; the knight on e3 and the light squares (f5, e4, g4) are worth more than a rook. } 19... f4 20. gxf4 Bh3 21. Ne3 Bxf1 22. Rxf1 Ng6 23. Bg4 { Key: a second exchange sacrifice; the Black queen and rooks are tied to f7 and d6. } 23... Nxf4 24. Rxf4 Rxf4 25. Be6+ Rf7 26. Ne4 Qh4 { Key: 30...Kxh8 31.Nxf7+ and 32.Nxg5 leaves White a piece up. } 27. Nxd6 Qg5+ 28. Kh1 Ra7 29. Bxf7+ Rxf7 30. Qh8+ 1-0

