1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 O-O 5. Bd3 d5 6. Nf3 c5 7. O-O Nc6 8. a3 Bxc3 9. bxc3 b6 10. cxd5 exd5 11. Bb2 { Key: Black fixes the queenside pawns and trades knights; White keeps the two bishops and a mobile centre. } 11... c4 12. Bc2 Bg4 13. Qe1 Ne4 14. Nd2 Nxd2 15. Qxd2 Bh5 16. f3 Bg6 17. e4 { Key: White's centre starts rolling; d5 and e6 are the threats. } 17... Qd7 18. Rae1 dxe4 19. fxe4 Rfe8 20. Qf4 b5 21. Bd1 Re7 22. Bg4 Qe8 23. e5 a5 24. Re3 Rd8 25. Rfe1 Re6 { Key: the exchange sacrifice: the e6-pawn and the knight coming to d5 blockade everything. } 26. a4 Ne7 27. Bxe6 fxe6 28. Qf1 { Key: Reshevsky returns the exchange to free his position. } 28... Nd5 29. Rf3 Bd3 30. Rxd3 cxd3 31. Qxd3 b4 { Key: a balanced ending; the sacrifice has done its job. } 32. cxb4 axb4 33. a5 Ra8 34. Ra1 Qc6 35. Bc1 Qc7 36. a6 Qb6 37. Bd2 b3 38. Qc4 h6 39. h3 b2 40. Rb1 Kh8 41. Be1 1/2-1/2

