1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 Nc6 13. d5 { Key: the centre is closed and the queenside pawn structure fixed; the a-file is the only open line. } 13... Nd8 14. a4 Rb8 15. axb5 axb5 16. b4 Nb7 17. Nf1 { Key: the bishop blocks the a-file so White can double rooks behind it; Black can never contest the file. } 17... Bd7 18. Be3 Ra8 19. Qd2 Rfc8 20. Bd3 g6 21. Ng3 Bf8 22. Ra2 c4 23. Bb1 Qd8 24. Ba7 Ne8 25. Bc2 Nc7 26. Rea1 Qe7 27. Bb1 { Key: White seals the kingside and trades Black's only active bishop. } 27... Be8 28. Ne2 Nd8 29. Nh2 Bg7 30. f4 f6 31. f5 g5 32. Bc2 Bf7 33. Ng3 Nb7 34. Bd1 h6 35. Bh5 Qe8 36. Qd1 { Key: Black can only shuffle the king: zugzwang in all but name. } 36... Nd8 37. Ra3 Kf8 38. R1a2 Kg8 39. Ng4 Kf8 40. Ne3 Kg8 41. Bxf7+ { Key: mate on g7 is unstoppable. } 41... Nxf7 42. Qh5 Nd8 43. Qg6 Kh8 44. Nh5 1-0

