1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. g3 Nc6 6. Bg2 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. Be3 c4 9. Ne5 O-O 10. b3 cxb3 11. Qxb3 Qb6 12. Rc1 Qxb3 13. axb3 Nb4 14. Na3 a6 15. Bd2 Rb8 16. Bxb4 Bxb4 17. Nd3 Bd6 18. Nc2 Bg4 19. Kf1 Bf5 20. Nc5 Rfc8 21. Ne3 Be6 22. b4 Kf8 23. Rc2 Ke7 24. Ke1 h5 25. Rb2 Rc7 26. Nd3 Ra8 27. b5 { Key: simplifications into a double-rook ending with Black's passed a- and b-pawns. } 27... a5 28. b6 Rc6 29. Rb5 a4 30. Nxd5+ Nxd5 31. Bxd5 Bxd5 32. Rxd5 Rxb6 33. Rxh5 Rb3 34. Kd2 b5 35. h4 Rc8 36. g4 a3 37. f4 Rcc3 38. Rd5 Ke6 39. Rh5 b4 40. Ra5 Rxd3+ 41. exd3 Bxf4+ 42. Ke2 Rc3 43. g5 Bc1 44. h5 { Key: White gives a rook for the b-pawn; both sides have passed pawns. } 44... b3 45. R5xa3 Bxa3 46. Rxa3 b2 47. Ra6+ Kf5 48. Rb6 Rc2+ 49. Ke3 Kxg5 50. d5 Kxh5 51. Kd4 g5 52. Rb8 g4 53. d6 Rc6 54. Ke5 Rc5+ 55. Kf6 g3 56. Rxb2 { Key: the g-pawn promotes: queen vs rook. } 56... Rd5 57. Kxf7 Rxd6 58. Rd2 Kg4 59. d4 Kf5 60. Ke7 Rd5 61. Rd3 Kf4 62. Ke6 Rg5 63. d5 Rg6+ 64. Ke7 g2 65. Rd1 Ke5 66. d6 Re6+ 67. Kd7 Rxd6+ 68. Rxd6 g1=Q 69. Re6+ { Key: the rook is lost after 79.Rh8 Qd6+ or 79.Rh1 Qd6+ 80.Kg8 Kg6. } 69... Kf5 70. Rd6 Qa7+ 71. Kd8 Ke5 72. Rg6 Qa5+ 73. Kd7 Qa4+ 74. Ke7 Qh4+ 75. Kf8 Qd8+ 76. Kf7 Kf5 77. Rh6 Qd7+ 78. Kf8 Kg5 0-1

