[Why "The most famous 19-move loss in history: Kasparov's move-order slip 7...h6?? allowed the known sacrifice 8.Nxe6!, and the Black king never escaped the centre. For students it is the standard Caro-Kann trap and a lesson in opening discipline."]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 { Key: the correct order is 7...Bd6 and only later ...h6. } 5. Ng5 Ngf6 6. Bd3 e6 7. N1f3 h6 8. Nxe6 { Key: the king is stuck in the centre for a knight. } 8... Qe7 9. O-O fxe6 10. Bg6+ Kd8 11. Bf4 { Key: every White piece joins; Black cannot coordinate. } 11... b5 12. a4 Bb7 13. Re1 Nd5 14. Bg3 Kc8 15. axb5 cxb5 16. Qd3 Bc6 17. Bf5 { Key: the queen is won back with a crushing position (19...bxc4 20.Qxc4 and the king falls). } 17... exf5 18. Rxe7 Bxe7 19. c4 1-0

